-    "content": "# [Informational] Enterprise Whitespace, Semantic Emojis, and Kanban Board\n\n## Overview\n\nHigh-performing engineering teams require interfaces that balance visual clarity with deep technical density. Cluttered, cramped dashboards create cognitive fatigue, while overly sparse designs hide crucial metadata. \ud83d\udc4dkanban delivers a refined **Enterprise Whitespace Design System**, combining generous breathing room with dense information display, sub-16ms drag-and-drop responsiveness, and the intuitive `<EmojiHint>` hover elaboration system.\n\n---\n\n## The Breathable Whitespace Design System\n\nThe visual design is grounded in CSS design tokens (`kanban/web/src/styles/tokens.css`):\n- **Predictable 4px / 8px Grid:** Consistent padding, gutter spacing, and card margins prevent visual clutter.\n- **High-Contrast Typography:** Clear typographic hierarchy using Inter and system font stacks for rapid scanning.\n- **Adaptive Light/Dark Modes:** Dark mode uses carefully calibrated slate and neutral backgrounds (`#0f172a`, `#1e293b`) with high contrast text (`#f8fafc`) to minimize eye strain.\n\n---\n\n## The `<EmojiHint>` Semantic Hover System\n\nTo keep cards concise without sacrificing context, \ud83d\udc4dkanban utilizes a standardized palette of 21 semantic emojis paired with instant hover elaboration tooltips:\n\n| Emoji Symbol | Semantic Meaning | Elaboration on Hover |\n| :---: | :--- | :--- |\n| `\ud83c\udff7\ufe0f` | Issue Identifier | Human-readable issue key and ticket URL |\n| `\ud83d\udd04` | Creator / Reporter | Author profile and ticket creation timestamp |\n| `\u26a1` | Priority | Corporate priority tier (Urgent, High, Medium, Low, None) |\n| `\u23f3` | Pending Transition | Active workflow transition helper or async gate |\n| `\ud83e\udd16` | Autonomous Agent | Agent service principal assignment or execution |\n| `\ud83d\udd12` | Parent Hierarchy | Parent issue or epic relationship |\n| `\ud83d\udd17` | Linked Object | Bidirectional dependency or related entity |\n| `\ud83e\uddea` | Custom Scripted Field | Sandboxed computed field with execution status |\n| `\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f` | Explicit Access | Access manifest and sharing permissions pill |\n| `\ud83d\udd14` | Subscription | Notification watcher status |\n| `\u2728` | Sparkle Completion | AI-assisted ghost text available |\n| `\ud83d\uded1` | Gate Veto | Transition rejected by rule or agent |\n\nHovering over any semantic emoji renders an instant, non-blocking tooltip detailing the exact state, owner, or timestamp without requiring extra clicks.\n\n---\n\n## Kanban Board View and Sub-16ms Drag-and-Drop\n\nThe Kanban Board provides a real-time, interactive visual pipeline of work across project states.\n\n![Kanban Board View](images/06-board-view.png)\n\n![Dark Theme Enterprise Kanban Board](images/22-dark-theme-board.png)\n\n### Board Architecture and Performance\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor User as Engineer / Operator\n    participant UI as React 19 Kanban Board\n    participant Store as Optimistic State Store\n    participant API as FastAPI Backend\n    participant WS as WebSocket Hub\n\n    User->>UI: Drag card from \"In Progress\" to \"Done\"\n    UI->>Store: Apply optimistic local mutation (<12ms)\n    Store-->>UI: Instantly re-render card in \"Done\" column\n    UI-->>User: Smooth 60 FPS visual feedback\n    Store->>API: PATCH /api/v1/issues/{id} (state: \"Done\")\n    alt Transition Accepted\n        API-->>Store: 200 OK & Updated Version ETag\n        API->>WS: Broadcast ISSUE_UPDATED event\n        WS-->>UI: Real-time sync to all other connected peers\n    else Transition Rejected / Gate Failed\n        API-->>Store: 409 Conflict / 422 Unprocessable\n        Store->>UI: Snap card back to \"In Progress\" with toast error\n    end\n```\n\n- **Sub-16ms Drag-and-Drop:** Built on lightweight HTML5 drag primitives paired with optimistic local UI mutations. When an operator moves a card across state columns, the card instantly re-renders in the destination column within 12 milliseconds, while the background API sync completes asynchronously.\n- **Virtualized Card Rendering:** Virtual scrolling allows columns to display thousands of tickets smoothly without degrading browser frame rates.\n- **State Columns:** Default workflow stages (`Backlog`, `Todo`, `In Progress`, `Done`, `Canceled`) with configurable WIP (Work In Progress) thresholds and visual warning indicators.\n- **2D Swimlane Grouping:** Operators can slice the board horizontally by Assignee, Priority, Module, or Sprint Cycle.\n\n![Filter Bar and 2D Swimlanes](images/29-filter-and-2d-swimlanes.png)\n\n---\n\n## The 5 Native View Layouts\n\nDifferent engineering disciplines need distinct perspectives on the same work graph. \ud83d\udc4dkanban provides 5 native views with instant zero-reload switching via URL query parameters (`?layout=`):\n\n![Multi-Layout Switching: List, Table, Calendar, Timeline](images/07-list-table-calendar-timeline.png)\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    Data[\"Universal Object Graph (Issues)\"] --> Layouts[\"5 Native Layout Projections\"]\n    Layouts --> Board[\"Board (?layout=board)<br/>Sub-16ms DnD, 2D Swimlanes, WIP Limits\"]\n    Layouts --> List[\"List (?layout=list)<br/>3-Pane Master-Detail, Keyboard Navigation\"]\n    Layouts --> Table[\"Table (?layout=table)<br/>Spreadsheet Grid, Multi-Select Bulk Actions\"]\n    Layouts --> Calendar[\"Calendar (?layout=calendar)<br/>Monthly/Weekly Grid, Date Drag Scheduling\"]\n    Layouts --> Timeline[\"Timeline (?layout=timeline)<br/>Gantt Dependencies, Critical Path Analysis\"]\n```\n\n![Global Command Palette for Rapid View Switching](images/23-command-palette.png)\n\n### 1. Board View (`?layout=board`)\nInteractive Kanban board with optimistic drag-and-drop, horizontal swimlanes, and live state columns.\n\n### 2. List View (`?layout=list`)\nA powerful three-pane split layout:\n- Left pane: Hierarchical navigation and filter presets.\n- Middle pane: High-density list with keyboard navigation (Up/Down arrows, Enter to view).\n- Right pane: Instant live ticket preview drawer without navigating away.\n\n### 3. Table View (`?layout=table`)\nSpreadsheet-style tabular editing:\n- In-place editing of titles, states, assignees, priorities, and dates.\n- Column reordering, visibility toggling, and multi-row selection for bulk updates.\n- Capability-gated cell editors: clicking a state or priority cell opens an active dropdown editor with instant optimistic UI feedback.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor User as Engineer / PM\n    participant Table as Table View Component\n    participant Cache as React Query / Local State\n    participant API as FastAPI Backend\n\n    User->>Table: Click State cell (e.g. \"Todo\" -> \"In Progress\")\n    Table->>Cache: Apply optimistic cell mutation (<10ms)\n    Cache-->>Table: Render updated state badge and progress ring\n    Table->>API: PATCH /api/v1/issues/{id} (state: \"in_progress\")\n    alt State Update Accepted\n        API-->>Cache: 200 OK with updated entity payload\n    else Conflict or Validation Failure\n        API-->>Cache: 422 Unprocessable / 409 Conflict\n        Cache-->>Table: Roll back cell value and show error toast\n    end\n```\n\n![Table View Inline Editing](images/37-table-inline-editing.png)\n\n### 4. Calendar View (`?layout=calendar`)\nMonthly and weekly scheduling grid:\n- Visualizes start dates, target delivery dates, and cycle deadlines.\n- Drag cards across dates to reschedule instantly.\n\n### 5. Timeline (Gantt) View (`?layout=timeline`)\nInteractive dependency and critical path visualization:\n- Displays `BLOCKS` and `BLOCKED_BY` dependency arrows between work items using high-performance SVG Bezier curves.\n- Shows dependency loops, schedule slippage, and critical path milestones.\n- Unified \"Today\" anchor button to snap view to the current date, with Day, Week, and Quarter zoom levels.\n- Toggle switch for \"Show BLOCKS arrows\" to declutter dense views on demand.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph TimelineEngine[\"Timeline Dependency Engine\"]\n        IssueA[\"Issue KAN-221<br/>Start: 2026-11-15 | Due: 2026-11-20\"]\n        IssueB[\"Issue KAN-212<br/>Start: 2026-11-21 | Due: 2026-11-28\"]\n        Bezier[\"SVG Bezier Dependency Curve<br/>typed BLOCKS object_link\"]\n        IssueA -->|BLOCKS| Bezier\n        Bezier -->|Target| IssueB\n    end\n```\n\n![Timeline View with BLOCKS Dependency Arrows](images/38-timeline-blocks-arrows.png)\n\n---\n\n## Project Settings Studios and Governance\n\nProject administrators configure project-level metadata, workflow states, and principal access through dedicated settings studios under `/projects/{project_key}/settings/`:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph ProjectSettings[\"Project Settings Studios\"]\n        General[\"General Settings (/settings)<br/>Identifier, Lead, Default Modules\"]\n        Workflows[\"Workflow States (/settings/workflows)<br/>States, Sequence, Colors, WIP Limits\"]\n        Members[\"Members & Access (/settings/members)<br/>Principals, Role Assignments, Explicit ACLs\"]\n    end\n```\n\n### General Settings and Default Modules\nConfigure project display name, identifier key prefix, lead owner, and default module attachments for incoming work items:\n\n![Project General Settings and Default Modules](images/54-project-settings-studio.png)\n\n### Workflow States and WIP Limits\nCustomize the state machine columns, sequence ordering, color badges, and column WIP (Work In Progress) thresholds:\n\n![Project Workflow States and WIP Limits](images/55-project-workflow-states-wip.png)\n\n### Project Members and Access ACL Management\nManage project collaborators across human users, groups, and autonomous agent service principals with granular capability masks:\n\n![Project Members and Access ACL Management](images/56-project-members-access-acl.png)\n"
