-    "content": "# [Architectural] System Topology and Multi-Container Architecture\n\n## Overview\n\nThe \ud83d\udc4dkanban platform is designed for operational flexibility and security hardening. It supports two primary deployment topologies:\n1. **Standalone Single-Container Mode (`docker run`):** A zero-dependency, turnkey distribution where the web application, FastAPI backend, and PostgreSQL 16 database run within a single container using an embedded Unix socket. Ideal for evaluation, air-gapped workstations, and single-host developer instances.\n2. **Multi-Container Production Stack (`docker compose`):** An enterprise-grade, five-network isolated container mesh designed for high availability, least-privilege service boundaries, and strict network compartmentalization.\n\nBoth deployment modes are built upon a clean monorepo architecture and adhere to a strict Apache-2.0 pure licensing mandate with zero AGPL, GPL, or SSPL runtime dependencies.\n\n---\n\n## Monorepo Code Organization\n\nThe platform source code is organized into modular packages:\n\n```\nkanban/\n|-- kanban/                  # FastAPI web server, REST API, WebSocket hub, content pipelines\n|   |-- api/v1/              # Versioned API routes (184 endpoints, OpenAPI 3.1.0)\n|   |-- auth/                # Multi-card authentication studio, session management, CSRF\n|   |-- content/             # Canonical Markdown normalizer, Unicode guards, hidden-DOM pruner\n|   |-- realtime/            # Distributed WebSocket hub, connection manager, event router\n|   `-- web/                 # React 19 single-page application (SPA) with Vite and Tailwind\n|-- database/                # Universal Object Graph, PostgreSQL schemas, and migrations\n|   |-- migrations/          # Alembic schema migrations (kanban_migrator)\n|   |-- models/              # SQLAlchemy 2.0 models with FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY\n|   `-- auditor/             # Universal object link integrity auditor and purger\n|-- mcp/                     # Three-surface Model Context Protocol server\n|   |-- surfaces/agent/      # /mcp/agent (9 execution & QA tools)\n|   |-- surfaces/docs/       # /mcp/docs (6 knowledge & sticky tools)\n|   |-- surfaces/admin/      # /mcp/admin (12 governance & lifecycle tools)\n|   `-- yaml_out.py          # InlineSafeDumper YAML serializer for token efficiency\n`-- agent/                   # Autonomous AI runtime and orchestration engine\n    |-- providers/           # Pluggable LLM clients (OpenAI, Ollama, Gemini)\n    |-- runners/             # Local CLI pipe harnesses (agy -p, codex -p) and mTLS runners\n    `-- sparkle/             # Inline cursor completion (FIM) and ghost-text engine\n```\n\n---\n\n## Standalone Single-Container Deployment (`docker run`)\n\nIn standalone mode, a single Docker container encapsulates the complete stack without requiring external database provisioning.\n\n```bash\ndocker run -d \\\n  --name thumbs-up-kanban \\\n  -p 8921:8921 \\\n  -v kanban_data:/var/lib/kanban/data \\\n  thumbs-up-kanban:latest\n```\n\n### Internal Unix-Socket Architecture\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph Standalone[\"Single Docker Container (thumbs-up-kanban:latest)\"]\n        Supervisor[\"PID-1 Process Supervisor (tini / Python supervisor)\"]\n        App[\"FastAPI Application Server<br/>(Port 8921 HTTP & WS)\"]\n        PG[\"Embedded PostgreSQL 16 Engine<br/>Unix Domain Socket (/var/run/postgresql/.s.PGSQL.5432)<br/>listen_addresses='' (Zero TCP Exposure)\"]\n        Storage[\"Volume Persistence Probe<br/>Mount: /var/lib/kanban/data\"]\n        \n        Supervisor --> App\n        Supervisor --> PG\n        App -->|Unix Domain Socket| PG\n        PG --> Storage\n    end\n```\n\nInside the standalone container:\n- **PID-1 Process Supervisor:** Manages the graceful startup, monitoring, and shutdown of both PostgreSQL and the ASGI application server.\n- **Embedded PostgreSQL 16:** Listens strictly on a local Unix domain socket (`/var/run/postgresql/.s.PGSQL.5432`). TCP networking for PostgreSQL is disabled (`listen_addresses = ''`), preventing network-level database intrusion.\n- **Volume Persistence Probe:** On startup, the container verifies that `/var/lib/kanban/data` is mounted to a persistent volume. If an ephemeral container filesystem is detected, the UI displays a dismissible amber warning banner alerting the operator to attach persistent storage before creating production data.\n- **Status and Health Panel:** Accessible at `/admin/standalone`, this panel reports database uptime, socket latency, storage utilization, and single-click export to multi-container Compose bundles.\n\n![Standalone Status Panel](images/04-standalone-status-panel.png)\n\n### Workspace Home and Initial State\n\nOnce the container finishes initialization, users land on the clean, breathable Workspace Home. The workspace view provides instant access to projects, work items, stickies, and system configuration.\n\n![Workspace Home](images/05-workspace-home.png)\n\n---\n\n## Multi-Container Production Architecture (`docker compose`)\n\nFor production environments, \ud83d\udc4dkanban deploys as a multi-container stack compartmentalized across five isolated Docker networks.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    Proxy[\"Reverse Proxy (Caddy / Nginx)\"] -->|edge_net| App[\"\ud83d\udc4dkanban App Container (FastAPI)<br/>- Uvicorn ASGI workers (UID 65532)<br/>- Multi-Card Auth & AAL2 Middleware<br/>- WebSocket Hub & Markdown Pipelines\"]\n    \n    App -->|data_net| PG[\"PostgreSQL 16 DB<br/>- FORCE RLS (100%)<br/>- pgvector + ltree<br/>- Isolated data_net\"]\n    App -->|sandbox_net| Sandbox[\"Sandbox Execution Runtime<br/>- Wasmtime runtime<br/>- nsjail runner<br/>- Zero data_net route\"]\n    App -->|egress_llm_net| AI[\"External AI Providers<br/>- OpenAI, Gemini<br/>- Local Ollama<br/>- mTLS repo runners\"]\n```\n\n![Standalone to Production Compose Export](images/27-standalone-compose-export.png)\n\n![System Settings and Production Diagnostics](images/26-system-settings.png)\n\n### The 5-Network Isolation Matrix\n\nTo prevent lateral movement and enforce zero-trust network boundaries, container communication is segregated into five distinct networks:\n\n| Network Name | Connected Services | Allowed Ingress / Egress | Security Rationale |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`edge_net`** | Reverse proxy, Web application | External HTTP/S traffic to port 8921 | Shields backend application from direct internet exposure; terminates TLS. |\n| **`app_net`** | Web application, Redis / cache (optional) | Inter-service caching and session distribution | Segregates application control plane from database and storage layers. |\n| **`data_net`** | Web application, PostgreSQL 16 | PostgreSQL TCP (port 5432) | Strictly internal. The database has zero external routing or internet gateway. |\n| **`sandbox_net`** | Web application, Custom Script runner | Unix socket / IPC pipe | Completely air-gapped. Scripts have zero route to `data_net` or the internet. |\n| **`egress_llm_net`** | Web application, LLM egress gateway | Outbound HTTPS to pinned AI API endpoints | Limits external outbound traffic exclusively to configured LLM APIs. |\n\n### Process Hardening and Least Privilege\n\nEvery container in the production stack enforces strict Linux security controls:\n- **Non-Root Execution:** Runs under dedicated unprivileged system users (`UID 65532`, `GID 65532`).\n- **Capability Dropping:** Drops all Linux capabilities on initialization (`--cap-drop=ALL`).\n- **No New Privileges:** Enforces `setpriv --no-new-privs` to prevent setuid privilege escalation.\n- **Read-Only Root Filesystem:** Container root filesystems are mounted read-only (`read_only: true`), with writable space restricted to tmpfs mounts for `/tmp` and `/run`.\n\n---\n\n## Supply Chain Integrity and Permissive Licensing\n\nIn strict accordance with enterprise governance requirements:\n- **Pure Apache-2.0:** All platform source code, libraries, and build targets are licensed under Apache-2.0.\n- **Zero Viral Licenses:** The dependency tree is continuously audited in CI to reject any runtime dependencies with copyleft licenses (GPL, AGPL, LGPL, SSPL).\n- **Pinned Dependencies:** All Python dependencies (`pyproject.toml`) and JavaScript packages (`package.json`) are cryptographically locked with exact hashes.\n"
