-    "content": "# [Informational] Ticket Screen, Peek Drawer, and Work Item Architecture\n\n## Overview\n\nThe ticket screen is the central operating surface for software engineering teams. \ud83d\udc4dkanban competes globally against Jira, Vibe Kanban, and legacy commercial trackers while eliminating context-switching friction through its high-performance **960px Ticket Peek Drawer** and keyboard-driven **Quick-Create Modal**.\n\n---\n\n## Quick-Create Work Item Modal (`C`)\n\nEngineers can capture issues rapidly from any screen in the application by pressing the keyboard shortcut `C` or clicking `+ New Work Item`.\n\n![Quick-Create Work Item Modal](images/08-quick-create-modal.png)\n\n### Key Capabilities of Quick-Create\n\n- **Keyboard Shortcut Driven:** Press `C` anywhere to open, `Escape` to dismiss, or `Ctrl+Enter` (`Cmd+Enter`) to submit.\n- **Draft Persistence (`\u270d\ufe0f Keep work-in-progress`):** Enabling the draft toggle preserves partial ticket text across navigation and browser restarts using local storage, preventing work loss.\n- **Inline Property Setting:** Assign status, priority, cycle, module, and assignees directly in the modal without secondary configuration.\n\n---\n\n## The 960px Ticket Peek Drawer (`?peek=`)\n\nClicking any card on the board or list opens the ticket in an expansive 960px side drawer while keeping the underlying board mounted and visible.\n\n![Ticket Peek Drawer with 17 Features](images/09-ticket-peek-drawer.png)\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph DrawerLayout[\"960px Ticket Peek Drawer Structure\"]\n        Header[\"Header Bar<br/>- Identifier (\ud83c\udff7\ufe0f) & Title<br/>- Subscribe (\ud83d\udd14), Copy Link (\ud83d\udd17)<br/>- Access Pill (\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f), Fullscreen Toggle\"]\n        \n        subgraph MainContent[\"Main Content Area\"]\n            Editor[\"ProseMirror Editor<br/>- Canonical UTF-8 Markdown<br/>- Sparkle FIM Completion (\u2728)<br/>- Live Mermaid & Media Rendering\"]\n            Subtasks[\"Sub-Issues & Checklists<br/>- Drag-and-drop reordering<br/>- Blocker resolution tracking\"]\n            Activity[\"4-Tab Activity Stream<br/>- All, Comments, History, \ud83e\udd16 Gates\"]\n        end\n        \n        subgraph PropertiesRail[\"Right-Hand Properties Rail\"]\n            StateProp[\"State & Workflow Transitions\"]\n            PriorityProp[\"Priority Tiering (Urgent..None)\"]\n            AssigneeProp[\"Assignees (Users, Groups, Agents)\"]\n            CycleProp[\"Cycle (Sprint) & Module Binding\"]\n            DatesProp[\"Start & Due Date Pickers\"]\n            CustomFields[\"Custom Scripted Fields (\ud83e\uddea)\"]\n            BlastRadius[\"Destructive Action Controls\"]\n        end\n    end\n    \n    Header --> MainContent\n    MainContent --- PropertiesRail\n```\n\n### Zero-Remount Architecture\n\n- **URL Synchronization:** Drawer state is synchronized with the URL (`/projects/KAN/issues?peek=KAN-12`). Refreshing or sharing the URL opens the exact drawer context.\n- **Background Preservation:** The underlying board does not unmount or reload. Users can interact with the drawer and return to their exact scroll position with zero latency.\n- **One-Click Fullscreen:** Operators can expand the drawer into a full-width page view for deep specification reading and back again seamlessly.\n\n---\n\n## Fullscreen Issue View and Authoring Studio\n\nWhen deep architectural work or comprehensive specification reading is required, operators can expand any ticket into the **Fullscreen Issue View** (`/projects/KAN/issues/{id}` or via the expand icon on the drawer header).\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph FullscreenView[\"Fullscreen Issue Studio Structure\"]\n        TopNav[\"Top Navigation Bar<br/>- Breadcrumb: Workspace / Project / Work Items<br/>- Key: KAN-142 | Copy ID | \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Access Inspector (Project + 2)<br/>- Subscribe Toggle (\ud83d\udd14) | Deep Link (\ud83d\udd17) | More Actions (...)\"]\n        \n        subgraph EditorColumn[\"Primary Specification & Activity Area\"]\n            Title[\"Issue Title Header with Inline Edit\"]\n            Desc[\"Rich Markdown Specification Body<br/>- Canonical CommonMark renderer<br/>- Mermaid diagram inline preview<br/>- Sparkle 320ms FIM ghost-text completion\"]\n            Toolbar[\"Rich Markdown Authoring Toolbar<br/>- Bold (B), Italic (I), Code (</>), Link, Image, Table, Mermaid\"]\n            CommentEditor[\"Comment Editor Box with Markdown and Mention Support\"]\n            ActivityTabs[\"4-Tab Activity Stream<br/>- All | Comments (N) | History | \ud83e\udd16 Gates (N)\"]\n        end\n        \n        subgraph SideRail[\"Right-Hand Metadata & Custom Fields Rail\"]\n            StandardFields[\"Standard Attributes<br/>- State, Priority, Assignees, Reporter<br/>- Start Date, Due Date, Module, Cycle\"]\n            CustomRail[\"Custom Fields Rail (Admin-Defined \ud83e\uddea)<br/>- CVSS Score (Severity Pill e.g. 8.8 High)<br/>- Target Environment, Build Number<br/>- Dynamic reload buttons per field\"]\n        end\n    end\n    \n    TopNav --> EditorColumn\n    EditorColumn --- SideRail\n```\n\n![Fullscreen Issue View with Rich Markdown Toolbar and Access Inspector](images/39-fullscreen-issue-view.png)\n\n### Key Fullscreen Features:\n1. **Rich Markdown Authoring Toolbar:** One-click formatting tools for bold, italics, inline code, links, quotes, tables, and Mermaid architecture diagrams.\n2. **Sparkle 320ms Fill-in-the-Middle (FIM):** Context-aware ghost text completions triggered as you write, dismissible with `Escape` and acceptable with `Tab` or right-click.\n3. **Effective Access Inspector (`\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f`):** Real-time badge computing combined project and issue-level permissions (`Project + 2`), showing inherited roles and explicit principal grants.\n4. **4-Tab Activity Stream:** Dedicated tabs for `All`, `Comments`, `History`, and `\ud83e\udd16 Gates` for isolated inspection of human discourse versus autonomous agent evaluations.\n5. **Custom Fields Rail:** Identical component and state rendering between peek drawer and fullscreen views, preserving field layout fidelity.\n\n---\n\n## The Complete 17 Enterprise Ticket Features\n\n\ud83d\udc4dkanban implements the full suite of 17 enterprise work item features (`8a` through `8q`):\n\n| # | Feature Identifier | Implementation Details |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1** | **Title & Canonical Description** | Rich Markdown editor supporting code blocks, tables, task lists, and Sparkle AI completion. |\n| **2** | **State Transition Selector** | Workflow-aware selector with synchronous Wasm validation and async AI gate interception. |\n| **3** | **Corporate Priority Tiering** | High-contrast visual badges: `Urgent` (red), `High` (orange), `Medium` (yellow), `Low` (blue), `None`. |\n| **4** | **Hybrid Assignees (`\ud83c\udff7\ufe0f`)** | Seamless assignment across individual human users, user groups, and autonomous agent service principals. |\n| **5** | **Created-by Reporter Badge (`\ud83d\udd04`)** | Immutable audit stamp recording the original creator and creation timestamp. |\n| **6** | **Dates & Scheduling** | Start date and Target delivery date pickers with automatic overdue highlighting and calendar sync. |\n| **7** | **Cycle (Sprint) Binding** | Direct assignment to active, upcoming, or backlog sprint cycles with automatic rollover. |\n| **8** | **Module Binding** | Grouping under functional modules with live roll-up progress bars and completion percentages. |\n| **9** | **Parent Hierarchy (`\ud83d\udd12`)** | Parent-child relationship binding with automated circular dependency rejection. |\n| **10** | **Sub-Issue Decomposition** | Nested sub-task checklist with drag reordering and progress tracking indicators. |\n| **11** | **Labels & Tagging** | Multi-colored semantic labels with workspace-level and project-level scopes. |\n| **12** | **Subscription Notifications (`\ud83d\udd14`)** | Watcher toggle delivering notifications on comments, state changes, and gate approvals. |\n| **13** | **Copy Link & Deep Linking (`\ud83d\udd17`)** | Generates canonical deep links directly to ticket headers or individual comments. |\n| **14** | **Explicit Sharing Pill (`\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f`)** | Visual indicator displaying the Access Manifest (principals, roles, and effective ACL masks). |\n| **15** | **Custom Scripted Fields (`\ud83e\uddea`)** | Dynamic fields computed by sandboxed Wasmtime/nsjail scripts with execution badges. |\n| **16** | **4-Tab Activity Feed** | Tabbed stream: `All`, `Comments` (with Markdown & mentions), `History` (audit trail), `\ud83e\udd16 Gates` (agent reviews). |\n| **17** | **Destructive Action Safety** | 2-stage blast-radius preview modal detailing affected children and links before archive or deletion. |\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Visual Inspection of Ticket Features\n\n### 4-Tab Activity Feed and Audit History\nThe activity feed separates human conversation from automated audit logs and AI agent gate reviews:\n\n![Activity Stream and Audit History](images/28-activity-stream-audit.png)\n\n<a id=\"modules\"></a>\n### Sprints, Cycles, and Functional Modules\nWork items bind directly to sprint cycles and functional modules with real-time velocity roll-ups:\n\n![Sprint Cycle Planning and Velocity Tracking](images/24-cycles-sprints.png)\n\n![Functional Module Hierarchy and Progress Tracking](images/25-modules-milestones.png)\n\n### Blast Radius Deletion Warning Modal\nTwo-stage deletion safety calculates the ripple impact across child issues, dependencies, and doc links:\n\n![Delete Blast Radius Warning Modal](images/20-delete-blast-radius.png)\n\n<a id=\"auto-archive\"></a>\n### Auto-Archive Policy\nWork items completed past the retention threshold are automatically moved to archive storage.\n"
