all Wiki topics, browser QA findings, and API/MCP schemas to identify missing features, incomplete items, and actionable backlog tickets. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. User Task Catalogue by Architecture Specification Section\n\n### Group A: Onboarding, Authentication & Standalone Operations (Spec S2, S3, S4)\n\n| Task ID | Spec Ref | User Persona | Task Title | Step-by-Step Human / Browser Verification Actions | Expected Outcome & Screenshot Target |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`UT-01`** | **S2.2, S4.2** | Platform Operator | **First-Boot `/setup` Claim Wizard** | 1. Navigate to `/setup` on a fresh instance.<br>2. Inspect the single-use `kb_setup_*` bootstrap token input, initial admin username/password fields, and workspace creation form.<br>3. Verify pre-session CSRF bootstrap (`__Host-kb_csrf` / `kb_csrf`). | Renders clean First-Boot Claim Wizard without 403 CSRF errors.<br>[images/01-first-boot-setup.png](images/01-first-boot-setup.png) |\n| **`UT-02`** | **S4.1, S4.3** | End User / Admin | **Multi-Card Login & Passkey/TOTP Prompt** | 1. Navigate to `/login`.<br>2. Verify ordered authentication cards (Local Admin, OIDC/OAuth2, LDAPS, WebAuthn Passkey `rp.name = \"\ud83d\udc4dkanban\"`).<br>3. Test credential entry and session establishment. | Displays enabled auth cards in `sort_rank` order with zero implicit email auto-merge.<br>[images/02-multi-card-login.png](images/02-multi-card-login.png) |\n| **`UT-03`** | **S4.4** | Server Admin (AAL2) | **Admin Auth Studio Management** | 1. Navigate to `/admin/auth`.<br>2. Inspect auth card list, enable/disable toggles, drag reorder, write-only secret fields, `Test Handshake` action, and `LOCKOUT_PREVENTED` break-glass guard. | Shows Auth Studio with mandatory vs. optional config sections and lockout guard.<br>[images/03-admin-auth-studio.png](images/03-admin-auth-studio.png) |\n| **`UT-04`** | **S2.2, S2.4** | Platform Operator | **Standalone Status Panel & Compose Export** | 1. Navigate to `/admin/standalone`.<br>2. Check volume persistence probe status (`/var/lib/kanban/data`), dismissible notification pill, encrypted backup trigger, and `docker-compose.yml` 5-network export tab. | Displays green/amber persistence status and copyable 5-network production Compose bundle.<br>[images/04-standalone-status-panel.png](images/04-standalone-status-panel.png) |\n\n![First-Boot Setup Wizard](images/01-first-boot-setup.png)\n\n![Multi-Card Login Screen](images/02-multi-card-login.png)\n\n---\n\n### Group B: Workspace Home, Multi-Layout Views & 17-Feature Ticket Screen (Spec S6, S7)\n\n| Task ID | Spec Ref | User Persona | Task Title | Step-by-Step Human / Browser Verification Actions | Expected Outcome & Screenshot Target |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`UT-05`** | **S6.1, S6.3** | Project Lead | **Workspace Home & Project Creation** | 1. Navigate to `/`.<br>2. Inspect project cards (`KAN`), quick-links (`Work Items`, `Board`, `Stickies`, `Docs`, `Custom Fields`), and click `+ Create Project` modal. | Renders Workspace Home grid and project creation modal.<br>[images/05-workspace-home.png](images/05-workspace-home.png) |\n| **`UT-06`** | **S6.2, S6.4** | Developer | **Kanban Board View & Optimistic Drag (`<12ms`)** | 1. Navigate to `/projects/KAN/issues?layout=board`.<br>2. Verify breathable whitespace, state columns (`Backlog`, `Todo`, `In Progress`, `Done`), corporate priority badges, `<EmojiHint>` hover tooltips, and card drag-and-drop. | Columns render with virtualized cards, semantic emojis, and instant drag response.<br>[images/06-board-view.png](images/06-board-view.png) |\n| **`UT-07`** | **S6.3** | Developer / PM | **Multi-Layout Switching: List, Table, Calendar & Timeline (Gantt)** | 1. Switch layouts via `?layout=list` (3-pane split view), `?layout=table`, `?layout=calendar`, and `?layout=timeline`.<br>2. Inspect filters bar, 2D swimlane grouping, and Gantt dependency arrows (`BLOCKS`). | All 5 layouts render cleanly without full-page reloads.<br>[images/07-list-table-calendar-timeline.png](images/07-list-table-calendar-timeline.png) |\n| **`UT-08`** | **S7.1, S7.2** | Developer | **Quick-Create Work Item Modal (`C`) & Draft Toggle** | 1. Press `C` or click `+ New Work Item`.<br>2. Enter title, Markdown description, state/priority, and inspect the `\u270d\ufe0f Keep work-in-progress` draft checkbox. | Opens Quick-Create modal and persists new issue into active view.<br>[images/08-quick-create-modal.png](images/08-quick-create-modal.png) |\n| **`UT-09`** | **S7.1-S7.4 (`8a`-`8q`)** | Developer / Reviewer | **Ticket Peek Drawer (`?peek=`) & 17-Feature Inspection** | 1. Click any issue card to open `?peek=KAN-1` while keeping the background board visible.<br>2. Verify properties rail (`State`, hybrid `Assignees \ud83c\udff7\ufe0f`, `Priority`, `Created-by \ud83d\udd04`, `Dates`, `Modules`, `Cycle`, `Parent \ud83d\udd12`, `Labels`).<br>3. Inspect header actions (`Subscribe \ud83d\udd14`, `Copy link \ud83d\udd17`, `Archive`, `Delete` blast-radius) and 4-tab Activity feed (`All`, `Comments`, `History`, `\ud83e\udd16 Gates`). | Background board stays mounted; drawer displays all 17 enterprise work-item features and Explicit Sharing pill.<br>[images/09-ticket-peek-drawer.png](images/09-ticket-peek-drawer.png) |\n\n![Kanban Board View](images/06-board-view.png)\n\n![Ticket Peek Drawer with 17 Features](images/09-ticket-peek-drawer.png)\n\n---\n\n### Group C: Canonical Markdown, Stickies, Docs & Sparkle (`\u2728`) AI Completion (Spec S5, S8, S9)\n\n| Task ID | Spec Ref | User Persona | Task Title | Step-by-Step Human / Browser Verification Actions | Expected Outcome & Screenshot Target |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`UT-10`** | **S8.2, S10.4** | Product Manager | **Workspace & Project Stickies + Smart AI Doc Promotion** | 1. Navigate to `/stickies` and `/projects/KAN/overview`.<br>2. Create a quick sticky note on the masonry grid.<br>3. Trigger **Promote to Doc** preview to verify AI structuring and ACL inheritance warning. | Sticky note renders on color-coded grid; promotion preview structures Markdown while preserving ACL scope.<br>[images/10-stickies-and-doc-promotion.png](images/10-stickies-and-doc-promotion.png) |\n| **`UT-11`** | **S8.1** | Technical Writer | **Hierarchical Docs (`ltree`), Outline & Version History** | 1. Navigate to `/projects/KAN/docs`.<br>2. Browse nested page tree, inspect auto-extracted heading outline rail, and view append-only version history/restore drawer. | Renders hierarchical doc tree, rich Markdown body, and version history diff/restore controls.<br>[images/11-docs-hierarchy-view.png](images/11-docs-hierarchy-view.png) |\n| **`UT-12`** | **S5.1-S5.4, S9.1-S9.3** | Engineer | **Canonical Markdown Editor, Mermaid Diagrams & Sparkle (`\u2728`) FIM** | 1. Open the editor (`/projects/KAN/docs` or `/__dev/editor`).<br>2. Test auto-converted paste, client-side Mermaid SVG rendering, and pause typing for `300ms` to trigger the blinking cursor Sparkle (`\u2728`) inline completion.<br>3. Test `Tab` or surgical right-click context menu accept. | Renders sanitized Markdown + Mermaid diagram and displays non-intrusive Sparkle ghost text.<br>[images/12-editor-mermaid-and-sparkle.png](images/12-editor-mermaid-and-sparkle.png) |\n\n![Project Stickies and Smart Promotion Modal](images/10-stickies-and-doc-promotion.png)\n\n![Editor with Mermaid Diagrams and Sparkle Completion](images/12-editor-mermaid-and-sparkle.png)\n\n---\n\n### Group D: MCP Access Studio, Custom Scripted Fields & Scripted Workflows (Spec S11, S13, S14)\n\n| Task ID | Spec Ref | User Persona | Task Title | Step-by-Step Human / Browser Verification Actions | Expected Outcome & Screenshot Target |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`UT-13`** | **S11.2, S11.3** | Developer / Admin | **Scopable MCP Keys, Per-Tool Toggles & Device Activation** | 1. Navigate to `/settings/mcp`, `/admin/mcp`, and `/activate` (RFC 8628 Device Flow).<br>2. Inspect hierarchical scoping (`Global`, `Workspace`, `Project`), expiration presets (including `Unlimited` with safety friction), and per-tool checkboxes across `/mcp/agent`, `/mcp/docs`, `/mcp/admin`. | Displays MCP Access Studio with copyable client config snippets and granular tool toggles.<br>[images/13-mcp-access-studio.png](images/13-mcp-access-studio.png) |\n| **`UT-14`** | **S13.1-S13.3** | Project / Server Admin | **Custom Scripted Fields (`\ud83e\uddea`) & Tiered Privilege Escalation** | 1. Navigate to `/projects/KAN/settings/custom-fields`.<br>2. Inspect custom field definitions, Wasm/script bindings, `\ud83e\uddea` computed badge on ticket rail, and AAL2 approval banner for escalated scope (`Project` -> `Workspace` -> `Server`). | Renders Custom Fields Studio and cryptographic admin approval status.<br>[images/14-custom-fields-studio.png](images/14-custom-fields-studio.png) |\n| **`UT-15`** | **S14.1-S14.4** | Workflow Architect | **Admin Workflow Transition Studio & Non-Persistent Dry-Run** | 1. Navigate to `/projects/KAN/settings/workflows`.<br>2. Select a `(from_state -> to_state)` rule, inspect ordered pipeline hooks (Tier A Wasm validator, Tier A mutator, Async Agent Transition Helper `in_app_sdk` / `cli_pipe` / `remote_runner`, mutable field checkboxes).<br>3. Open the **Dry-Run Drawer**, test against a sample ticket, and inspect per-step execution results and copyable `kanban-agent validate-transition` CLI snippet. | Displays pipeline ordering studio and executes zero-persistence dry-run with step timings.<br>[images/15-workflow-transition-studio.png](images/15-workflow-transition-studio.png) |\n| **`UT-16`** | **S14.2** | Developer | **Async Agent Gate Lifecycle on Board (`\u23f3\ud83e\udd16` -> `\ud83d\uded1\ud83e\udd16` / `\u2705\ud83e\udd16`)** | 1. Inspect async agent gate card states (`/projects/KAN/issues?layout=board` or `/__dev/realtime`): live countdown timer (`\u23f3\ud83e\udd16`), `240ms` spring snap-back toast on veto (`\ud83d\uded1\ud83e\udd16`), and verified header badge (`\u2705\ud83e\udd16`). | Visualizes pending agent hold, countdown progress bar, and veto snap-back toast.<br>[images/16-async-agent-gate-states.png](images/16-async-agent-gate-states.png) |\n\n---\n\n### Group E: Administrative Hardening, RBAC & Gate Rework Verification (Spec S3, S4, S11, S14)\n\n| Task ID | Spec Ref | User Persona | Task Title | Step-by-Step Human / Browser Verification Actions | Expected Outcome & Screenshot Target |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`UT-17`** | **S2.2, S4.4, S15.1** | Server Admin (AAL2) | **Admin Browser QA: Auth Studio, Principals & Favicon** | 1. Navigate to `/admin/auth`.<br>2. Inspect multi-card authentication ordering and lockout protection.<br>3. Inspect Principal Management kind filter tabs (`ALL`, `USER`, `GROUP`, `AGENT`).<br>4. Click `+ Create Principal`, select `GROUP` or `AGENT`, provide identifier and display name, and submit.<br>5. Verify `GET /favicon.ico` returns HTTP 200 with `Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400`. | Auth Studio manages USER/GROUP/AGENT principals; `/favicon.ico` serves branded asset cleanly.<br>[images/17-admin-browser-qa.png](images/17-admin-browser-qa.png) |\n| **`UT-18`** | **S3.1-S3.4, S13.2, S15.2** | Standard Member | **Standard User Browser QA & Negative RBAC Isolation** | 1. Authenticate as standard workspace member (`WORKSPACE_MEMBER`).<br>2. Browse assigned projects, board, list, docs, and ticket drawer.<br>3. Attempt navigation to administrative routes (`/admin/auth`, `/admin/standalone`, `/admin/mcp`, `/projects/KAN/settings/custom-fields`).<br>4. Verify custom fields editor fails closed with access denied toast/banner.<br>5. Confirm zero administrative controls or privileged mutation buttons leak into client DOM. | Negative RBAC strictly isolates standard users; privileged views fail closed without privilege leaks.<br>[images/18-standard-user-negative-rbac.png](images/18-standard-user-negative-rbac.png) |\n| **`UT-19`** | **S11.1-S11.4, S14.3** | Security Architect / Agent | **CLI MCP Scoping Matrix & E2E Gate Rework Loop** | 1. Audit all 12 `/mcp/admin` tools in `mcp/auth.py` for action-aware scope enforcement (`admin:read`, `admin:write`, `admin:destructive`).<br>2. Verify `project` argument alias to `project_key` on `manage_ai_and_agent_runners` and `architect_project`.<br>3. Verify OpenAI Codex CLI invocation enforces `codex exec -s read-only -` and rejects `-p`.<br>4. Run E2E transition gate rework loop: first transition enters `pending_agent` (`\u23f3\ud83e\udd16`), verifier rejects initial commit SHA with `cited_files`, rolls back to source state (`\ud83d\uded1\ud83e\udd16`), developer commits rework fix, and second transition evaluates fixed commit SHA, records `verdict=\"APPROVE\"` (`\u2705\ud83e\udd16`), advancing state and appending immutable hash-chained audit record. | Full 12-tool scope matrix enforced; E2E gate rework loop executes and logs immutable provenance.<br>[images/19-mcp-scoping-and-rework-loop.png](images/19-mcp-scoping-and-rework-loop.png) |\n\n![Workflow Transition Studio and Dry-Run Drawer](images/15-workflow-transition-studio.png)\n\n![Async Agent Gate Card States and Snap-Back Lifecycle](images/16-async-agent-gate-states.png)\n"
